<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding a conditional probability of the product of 2 dice throws</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Two fair dice are thrown and the product of the numbers on the dice is recorded. Given that one die lands on {@one_die@}, find the probability that the product on the dice is</p>
<p>(a) Exactly {@exact_product@} = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) More than {@more_than_product@} = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Remember that the probability of an event \(B\) occurring given that event \(A\) has occurred is denoted as \(P(B|A)\) and is calculated as follows: \(P(B|A)=\frac{P(B|A)}{P(A)}\). This is known as conditional probability. </p>
<p>Also, keep in mind that the probability space for this question can be represented in a table as shown.</p>
